# Diffalo reviews in this app — no accounts, no fixed fire URL

The generic Diffalo skill tells agents to "mint a fresh account" for the state command. That instruction is wrong here and caused a failed review.

- **Never emit `account`.** This SPA has no sign-in. An `account` field makes Diffalo demand a sign-in command that does not exist.
- **Never emit `clientState`.** Diffalo refuses it without an account today. Delete this line once Diffalo supports account-less `clientState`.
- **Never invent a fire slug, and never pin one in `diffalo.json`.** Which fires are active changes daily. `scripts/diffalo-state.mjs` picks one at run time from the live fire API. `routeKey` is an exact pathname match, so a `places.fire` or `recordable.routes["/fire/…"]` entry goes stale within weeks and the gate then applies the home tagline to a fire page — a 90-second timeout.
- **Fire stories use `state: { name: "fire-detail" }` and no `place`.** A state's route wins over `place` and `startRoute`, and there is deliberately no `fire` place to name.
- **Global `expectText` is the `<title>`, on purpose.** It feeds the dump-dom gate (`--dump-dom --disable-gpu`, tags stripped, `<title>` included) and means "the SPA shell loaded", not "the map is up". Per-route `expectText` *replaces* the global list, so only static pages get stronger text.
- **Map readiness goes in the state command's `ready` field**, which the recording browser waits on: `rd-fire-perimeter` (perimeter GeoJSON has landed) or `rd-fire-shell` (chrome mounted, map may still be empty). A post-mount string in `expectText` burns 90 seconds and fails.
